  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: ClinRC 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'After enrolling in a clinical trial, a patient has questions about upcoming
    visits, what to expect during certain tests, and who to contact if concerns come
    up between appointments.


    <b>During a clinical trial, research coordinators
    help support participants by serving as a point of contact and helping them understand
    study procedures.</b>

    

    Is this <b>true</b> or <b>false?</b>'
  explanation: During clinical trials, research coordinators often serve as a key
    point of contact for patient participants. They help explain study procedures,
    answer questions, coordinate schedules, and provide ongoing support so patients
    feel informed and supported throughout the study. This helps reduce confusion
    and ensures patients know where to turn if questions or concerns come up.
  correctAnswer: True
  incorrectAnswer1: False
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Research Coordinator
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Clinical
